## Problem Statement
Consider a factory with a manufacturing process consisting of n sequential stations. Every task entering the system must pass through all stations, from 1 to n, in order to be completed. The factory has two parallel production lines, and a task may switch from one line to the other between consecutive stations. Let t_{ij}, $1 \le i \le 2, 1 \le j \le n$, denote the processing time required at station j of production line i, and let $c_j$, $1 \le j \le n$ denote the time required to switch production lines before entering station j. The goal is to determine how to process a task in order to minimize the total time required.

